{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554912320,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MTc1NDU2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3313#issuecomment-481754564"},"message":"It looks like coverage for **test** files isn't reported for AppVeyor.  That explains the lack of coverage observed in gh-3307 to the degree I care to dig.  Of course it'd be good to know why this happens and how to fix it, but I'm not planning to look into that anytime soon, if ever.\n\n--- \n\nMy statement above is based on the following observations:\n\n  * The AppVeyor-only codecov report for f802738 does report some amount of coverage, so coverage reporting from AppVeyor isn't failing entirely.\n\n    https://codecov.io/gh/datalad/datalad/tree/f80273868482df1b00d8cfb5369eb3270ef233f6\n\n  * The AppVeyor-only codecov report for f802738 doesn't list test files or test directories.  For example, the `datalad/interface/` directory [listing for f802738][0] (again, no contribution from Travis) lacks a test directory while the [listing for 73145b4][1] (a combination of Travis and AppVeyor) has a `tests/`.\n\n  * Outside of tests, I can find code under `on_windows` that is covered.  Here's an [example in annexrepo.py][2].\n\n[0]: https://codecov.io/gh/datalad/datalad/tree/f80273868482df1b00d8cfb5369eb3270ef233f6/datalad/interface\n[1]: https://codecov.io/gh/datalad/datalad/tree/73145b49d55fa2fc24139a45df0432a02fa56909/datalad/interface\n[2]: https://codecov.io/gh/datalad/datalad/src/f80273868482df1b00d8cfb5369eb3270ef233f6/datalad/support/annexrepo.py#L3293","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554912592,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjI2NjYyMDUyNA=="},"status":2},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1554919757,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4MTgwMTQ2Ng==","github-url":